From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:33:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Check and store a put's index keys with one
 statement per table

A put checked each key of a unique index with its own SELECT and
inserted each index key with its own INSERT, so a record with ten
multiEntry keys cost ten more statements; at 0.2-0.3 ms per RDB statement
on the DAYU200 that made indexed puts slow (P3 review S1). A put now
checks the keys of each unique index with one value IN (...) statement
(500 keys per statement) and inserts the records of each index table
with one multi-row INSERT (200 rows per statement), as the index
population already did; set_index_keys shares the two helpers.

A put with a generated key skips the check whether a record with its key
exists: the key generator's current number is above every number key in
the store, since storing a key possibly updates the generator, so no
record can have it.

Validation: `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits` (host SQLite): 143 passed, 1 skipped, with test_put_index_records_of_many_keys (700 keys of a unique multiEntry index and 300 of another per record, a taken key found in the second check, an overwrite with its own keys) and the unique-index and population tests; `./mach check --ohos -- -p servo-storage --all-targets --no-default-features --features ohos-rdb-backend` and `cargo clippy -p servo-storage --lib -- -D warnings`: no warnings. DAYU200 (QuickJS + RDB, checked-release), 2,000 puts each, this commit vs the previous one: 395 -> 579/s with a multiEntry index of 10 keys per record, 1,225 -> 1,876/s with generated keys and no index, 933 -> 953/s with one unique index, 1,805 -> 1,860/s without an index. The WPT runs of the series are in the last commit of the series (P4.2).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; batched the statements, added the backend test, measured puts on the board)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
